1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,311
The first pressure came from a reference in an annual report.

2
00:00:03,311 --> 00:00:09,900
A quotation from their own study had been used to support a conclusion they had never drawn.

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:15,405
“This is a terrible thing to happen to a young project,” Maya said.

4
00:00:15,405 --> 00:00:22,949
“It is also a chance to practice precision.” All of them felt the chill of it.

5
00:00:22,949 --> 00:00:30,919
They heard the same complaint from a military institute, a laboratory, and a casual reader of the student journal.

6
00:00:30,919 --> 00:00:36,183
Each wanted a complete list; none wanted an observation.

7
00:00:36,183 --> 00:00:40,238
“A form is not a structure,” Lin said.

8
00:00:40,238 --> 00:00:53,437
“A structure holds weight.” Amongst the art on the wall, a boy from the school of education had pinned a note: experience without method is only memory.

9
00:00:53,437 --> 00:00:59,551
The weak point was the second edition, distributed in a batch of two hundred.

10
00:00:59,551 --> 00:01:13,410
On the editing table, amongst the crumbs of bread, a ghost of the old text survived — a stray adjective, a missing noun, one line about coordination that nobody could explain.

11
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:19,305
“We must identify it before we produce the next printing,” she said.

12
00:01:19,305 --> 00:01:23,015
“Up to now we have been lucky.”

13
00:01:23,015 --> 00:01:27,794
A smile from Professor Zhao did not soften the news.

14
00:01:27,794 --> 00:01:37,838
The institute wanted a new edition within a minute of the review, and the sensitive material — the quotations from named students — had to be removed.

15
00:01:37,838 --> 00:01:40,783
The spell of good humour broke.

16
00:01:40,783 --> 00:01:46,173
“You cannot manipulate a quotation into consent,” she said.

17
00:01:46,173 --> 00:01:51,223
“That is not innovation, it is decoration.”

18
00:01:51,223 --> 00:01:59,737
Here the ignorance of the outside world became useful: nobody had told them that such a correction was impossible.

19
00:01:59,737 --> 00:02:07,816
A historical note belonged in the appendix, and they would inform every reader of the correction in a separate letter.

20
00:02:07,816 --> 00:02:19,645
“This particular error,” Lin wrote in the margin, “is why we keep everything.” Further work was for the reader to compare, not for the author.

21
00:02:19,645 --> 00:02:30,339
The new letter would go from the office to every reader; it would lead with the correction, explain why it mattered, and use one word instead of ten.

22
00:02:30,339 --> 00:02:34,619
They had to learn that a correction is also information.

23
00:02:34,619 --> 00:02:38,979
“Remember the first line,” he told the group.

24
00:02:38,979 --> 00:02:44,471
“Other people will read the rest, without us.”
